      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes it is possible to set these in BUILD.gn [1] and Bazel [2] builds however we currently have conversion disabled for all our files because there were too many places to fix if we turned them on (and IIRC, there were a few places we did this for a good reason).\n\nI\u0027d be curious to try just the `-Wconversion` since the other two should be on in Skia itself, but I suppose they might not be on in Chromium?\n\nIn any case, this is a fine spot to add such a check to incrementally add support for the warning. Idea (which I will sketch out in a new CL): condense this into a macro so we can roll out this and other warnings to other .cpp files similarly.\n\n[1] https://github.com/google/skia/blob/2d31a2a0ede9b4cbf38c9a1d8598427f2921f293/gn/skia/BUILD.gn#L531\n[2] https://github.com/google/skia/blob/2d31a2a0ede9b4cbf38c9a1d8598427f2921f293/include/config/copts.bzl#L96",
